Z||000003||bHooper||04-01-2000||09:59 PM||||well, i called around to 2 sears' and every store, to no success.  however, when we went to go get a fuel filter, at auto zone, for my budies SE... shat did I see setting on the shelf?  is that... could that... it is!! a shiney new 16x18mm flare nut wrench!<P>unfortunately, we had done such a lousey job earlier, all the corners are rounded  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>wound up losening the nut under the mainfold for hte feed and at the hose from the tank for the "return"||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||04-02-2000||12:29 AM||||one of those sears "clench wrench" or "robo grip" pliers might get the rounded nuts. You want to replace those if you can. I've looked at both. They should get a better bit than "vise grips." Vice Grips have a nasty habit of squashing flair nuts out of round if not very carefully adjusted.||||reg||1
